      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. Travel from La Paz via Tiwanaku to the Peruvian border at Desaguadero, then transfer to your hotel in Puno. In the afternoon, visit the Uros Islands on Lake Titicaca. Overnight in Puno."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:aed712561743a8d2",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "652e5a8d63d1031a367009a298c23e2608ae20f8d4a5a5e6edecc32de6f82cb5",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-20261110-mw9trx1d-qy2ds2",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "We head towards the Peruvian border, where the famous Lake Titicaca lies. On the way, we visit the imposing ruins of Tiwanaku, the remains of one of South America's oldest civilisations. You will see the Gate of the Sun, the Kalasasaya Temple and the pyramids, monuments to Tiwanaku's past. The people of Tiwanaku were skilled in agriculture, water engineering, architecture, medicine and social organisation. Natural upheavals, including long periods of drought, brought about the collapse of Tiwanaku towards the end of the first millennium CE, after which the civilisation mysteriously disappeared. The tour ends in the border town of Desaguadero, where a transfer takes you to your hotel in Puno."
